141	     * preserved), except that its line breaks &mdash; a lone {@code \r}, a lone {@code \n}, or a {@code \r\n} pair
142	     * &mdash; are each normalized to {@code \r\n}, as a browser does before submitting. This does not modify the
143	     * textarea's DOM text. Field names and the values of inputs, options and files are left untouched.</p>
144	     * <p>In addition to the form's descendant controls, controls elsewhere in the same Document that carry a
145	     * {@code form} attribute whose value is this form's {@code id} are submitted as well (matching the browser's
146	     * <a href="https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/form-control-infrastructure.html#association-of-controls-and-forms">
147	     * form-associated elements</a> rules). All controls are merged in document order. A control with a {@code form}
148	     * attribute is handled solely by that explicit association, even when it is also a descendant: an unresolvable
149	     * value (no such id, the target is not a form, or an earlier form in the Document shares this id) excludes it.
150	     * Forms without an id absorb no external controls.</p>
